From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jianfeng Liu <Jianfeng.Liu@cixtech.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/92] drm: widen the plane mask to 64 bits

drm_plane_mask() returns a u32 and drm_crtc_state.plane_mask is a u32, so a
device with more than 32 planes cannot be described: 1 << index is undefined
for index >= 32 (on arm64 the shift wraps, so plane 32 alias plane 0) and the
CRTC state silently drops the high bits.  linlondp registers up to 40 planes
for a display cluster (5 DPUs x 2 pipelines x 4 layers).

Widen drm_plane_mask() to u64 (1ULL) and drm_crtc_state.plane_mask to u64,
raise the plane index limit from 32 to 64 accordingly, and widen the places
that keep the mask in a local variable or print it.

This is the core half of the change needed by the 26q2 linlondp merge in
00101; it can be dropped once the equivalent change lands upstream.
